{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "a8ca1f73-26d7-42b0-b3c4-94f2429cc556",
    "name": "Rudder - Ticket Management API",
    "description": "## 🎫 Rudder API Collection\r\n\r\nThis collection provides a comprehensive set of endpoints to interact with the **Rudder Ticket Management System**. It covers everything from basic CRUD operations to advanced dashboard analytics.\r\n\r\n### 🚀 Getting Started\r\n1. Ensure your local server is running at `http://localhost:3000` (or update the `BASE_URL` variable).\r\n2. Use the **Tickets** folder for core data operations.\r\n3. Use the **Statistics** folder to fetch analytical data for dashboards.\r\n\r\n### 🛠️ Key Features\r\n- **Full CRUD Support:** Create, Read, Update, and Delete tickets.\r\n- **Automated Tests:** Status code and schema validation scripts included.\r\n- **Variable Management:** Uses collection-level variables for easy environment switching.\r\n- **Rich Documentation:** Detailed field descriptions and example responses.\r\n\r\n### 👨‍💻 Developer\r\nDeveloped and maintained by **Ozan Demircan**.\r\nCheck out more projects on GitHub: [github.com/ozandmrcn](https://github.com/ozandmrcn)",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "40788805"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Tickets",
      "description": "Handles all core ticket operations. Each ticket document contains:\r\n- `title`: Short summary (String)\r\n- `description`: Detailed issue info (String)\r\n- `category`: [Software, Hardware, Connection, Other]\r\n- `priority`: 1 (Very Low) to 5 (Critical)\r\n- `progress`: 0-100 percentage\r\n- `status`: [Pending, In Progress, Resolved]",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get All Tickets",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"Response has success flag\", function () {",
                  "    const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.success).to.be.true;",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "description": "Fetches the list of all tickets available in the system. Perfect for populating grid views or lists.",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{BASE_URL}}/api/tickets",
              "host": [
                "{{BASE_URL}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "tickets"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Create Ticket",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Ticket Created Successfully\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (jsonData.newTicket && jsonData.newTicket.id) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"LAST_TICKET_ID\", jsonData.newTicket.id);",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"title\": \"Network Connectivity Issue\",\n    \"description\": \"Unable to connect to the internal VPN since morning update.\",\n    \"category\": \"Connection Issue\",\n    \"priority\": 4,\n    \"progress\": 0,\n    \"status\": \"Pending\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Registers a new ticket in the database. \r\n\r\n**Validation Rules:**\r\n- `title`: Required\r\n- `priority`: Must be 1-5\r\n- `progress`: Must be 0-100",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{BASE_URL}}/api/tickets",
              "host": [
                "{{BASE_URL}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "tickets"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
